@*
  The representative h-card. It appears in the footer of every page, but it is
  the copy on the home page that counts: an h-card is "representative" of a URL
  when its u-url matches that URL and carries rel=me, which is what makes this
  the answer to "who is https://stuff.interfree.ca/?".

  The properties are spelled out rather than left implied. Implied name and
  photo only apply to an h-card whose only child is a single img or a, and this
  one has both a photo and a name, so implying would have silently dropped the
  photo.

  The photo has empty alt on purpose: the name it illustrates is right beside
  it, so repeating it would just be read twice.
*@
<div class="h-card author-card">
  <a class="u-url u-uid" rel="me" href='@Context.GetLink("/", true)'>
    <img class="u-photo" src='@Context.GetLink(Context.GetString("AuthorPhoto", "/img/photo.jpg"))' alt="" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto;">
    <span class="p-name">@Context.GetString(WebKeys.Author)</span>
  </a>
</div>
